{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head b7be6f69b7f41698fb8bdfc7a8e7c9aab519c89d on builder/nf11-witness-poll-20261117, all 5 artifacts, for request 8c586d99 under my promise 3050232c. The implementation is NF-11 (request 39152cbb, promise a4c3cf88). The reporting artifact is the NF-11 note. Main d910468d is an ancestor.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The note first, then the whole diff.\n- `witness-poll.mjs`. `pollUntil(read, holds, { what, timeout, interval })` awaits each read before it judges the value. It returns the first value that holds and lets a read's throw end the wait. Once the time has passed, a value that does not hold ends the wait with an error that names `what`. The loop sleeps `interval` between reads.\n- `custody-witness.mjs`. The Check wait now polls `records()` for up to 60 s until a record has phase `accepted`. `records()` keeps the old wait's scope filter: it returns only the records whose `identity.target.scope` equals the target. The two lock-queue waits now poll `page.evaluate(... navigator.locks.query() ...)` with `Boolean`. Every remaining `waitForFunction` predicate is synchronous: the voice option and the `witness` global.\n- The old Check predicate resolved `false` when IndexedDB failed to open. `records()` rejects instead, so a custody failure now ends the wait with its error and does not wait out the timeout.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The red. `2026-11-17-nf11-red/red-unawaited-read.txt` runs the three tests against a poll that judges the unawaited read, as Playwright does. 2 fail and 1 passes.\n- Run 6. `2026-11-17-nf7-counter-witness-run6/report.json` reports mode `hosted-counter` with no failures. After the lost reply it kept 1 record in phase `unknown` with 1 POST. After Check it kept 1 record in phase `accepted` with 1 POST, 1 journal entry, and `sameEnvelope` true. Run 6 ran from cca2bfab, which differs from this head only in the note.\n- The gate. END b8750d44 passed at this head. The last lines of `gate.txt` read \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- Scope. The 5 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only d910468d b7be6f69`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n- Wake rate. The head changes only test code. It adds no alarm, retry or scheduled pass to any Worker.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The fault was in the witness, and the fix stays in the witness. Node owns the wait, so the result no longer depends on how Playwright treats a returned Promise. With this head, run 6 is the first hosted run whose Check result means what it says.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The head changes no runtime code. The witness reads the same custody records as before, and the private failure note and its redaction do not change.\n\nSimplification: no required change. When a read is slow, the wait can run up to one read past its timeout, which is harmless for a witness.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8c6531892773dc4253cf3d9346924b825524b7ba","binding":"assigned","head":"b7be6f69b7f41698fb8bdfc7a8e7c9aab519c89d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3050232cfa967b53c05bd06206872ba2f31d581e\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a4c3cf88d40bdbe4521c7ef996e48ab616ed5390\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3050232cfa967b53c05bd06206872ba2f31d581e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}